                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "36ce4c7e-f442-3c57-9404-bffb4883a0f7",
                        "entry_id": "bdf543d2-ddc3-3ace-b09d-e946ac31a022",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To earn back something one has lost."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "48e2539a-ba06-4620-999c-e712242d82e1",
                                "sense_id": "36ce4c7e-f442-3c57-9404-bffb4883a0f7",
                                "text": "What's the point in telling somebody that they now have a chance to go for a huge bonus when by scrolling the message slowly across the display the ball is already lost - meaning the bonus has to be re-earnt?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "76e14982-490b-4d87-afa1-8e1d42b3d8cc",
                                "sense_id": "36ce4c7e-f442-3c57-9404-bffb4883a0f7",
                                "text": "It is the narcotic of the football itself that draws people in, makes them travel miles from home on wet nights, part with money that will have to be re-earnt at the workplace the next day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "277765ee-1bb5-423f-8da6-b3746be91755",
                                "sense_id": "36ce4c7e-f442-3c57-9404-bffb4883a0f7",
                                "text": "Your culture used to know its job; now you're changing that job, and it has to relearn then re-earn its competence."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d00c83e8-5a96-4f9c-8007-f6fc27c192d7",
                                "sense_id": "36ce4c7e-f442-3c57-9404-bffb4883a0f7",
                                "text": "Trust can be re-earnt just as it can be destroyed."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5671c8b0-57aa-3f01-91a2-259ebc04e191",
                        "entry_id": "bdf543d2-ddc3-3ace-b09d-e946ac31a022",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To repeat the process of earning; to renew one's status as deserving."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9f8cd0c0-a32e-4032-b781-53494b310f35",
                                "sense_id": "5671c8b0-57aa-3f01-91a2-259ebc04e191",
                                "text": "The humble brand understands that it needs to re-earn attention, re-earn loyalty, and reconnect with its audience as if every day is the first day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0962f5ec-7528-4306-99fd-de8adf56f527",
                                "sense_id": "5671c8b0-57aa-3f01-91a2-259ebc04e191",
                                "text": "To do this, we understood that we had to earn and re-earn our hospitality reputation every day, one customer at a time, 50 million times a day."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6aeac82c-c11e-4c56-9454-2e33c332bd89",
                                "sense_id": "5671c8b0-57aa-3f01-91a2-259ebc04e191",
                                "text": "After his family moved to Australia five years ago, and he re-earnt his black belt in the Australian system, Teo began competing in local and state competitions, quickly getting strong results."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
